BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Journey to Space" Ribbon Cutting
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261114T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T191221Z
UID:e1ad88b2e4e6141d76def5b6fe3377@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Journey to Space Ribbon Cutting and Exhibit Opening Saturday\,
  November 14\, 2026 11:00am – 11:30am The EcoTarium is excited to announ
 ce our newest traveling exhibit\, Journey to Space . Come to the official 
 opening and ribbon cutting on Saturday\, November 14\, 2026 at 11:00 am an
 d be among the first to experience this exciting new interactive exhibit! 
 Visitors will discover and explore the exciting environment of outer space
  in Journey to Space ! This highly interactive experience utilizes hands-o
 n elements that allow visitors to work with drop towers\, water rockets\, 
 and robotic arms\, while educating on topics like artificial gravity\, orb
 ital physics\, Newton’s third law of motion\, and more! There’s much t
 o discover as visitors learn more about these immersive topics which explo
 re a variety of challenges and accomplishments\, and show how far we have 
 come in the last fifty years of exploring space. Can’t make our event? D
 on’t worry! We always have something new happening outside\, inside\, an
 d onstage. The Journey to Space exhibit will be sticking around until Apri
 l 2027! Come check it out or experience one of our daily planetarium progr
 ams*\, take a ride on the seasonal Worcester Railers Explorer Express Trai
 n*\, and get up close to our resident otters*! * Requires a separate ticke
 t that is not included with admission. Learn More about the exhibit! This 
 exhibit is included with admission to the EcoTarium on weekdays. On weeken
 ds\, a ticket is required for entry into the Stoddard Exhibition Hall for 
 this exhibit. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://
 www.discovercentralma.org/event/journey-to-space-ribbon-cutting/31017/\n\n
 Events Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Loc
 al fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discov
 ercentralma.org/event/journey-to-space-ribbon-cutting/31017/
LOCATION:EcoTarium\, 222 Harrington Way\, Worcester\, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/journey-to-space-ribbon-cuttin
 g/31017/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Making Paleolithic Cave Art: Teen Saturdays Workshop
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261212T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T191221Z
UID:9287acf8fff8ade7a1f1040c186134@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Journey 30\,000 years into the past to discover how ancient hu
 mans used art to express themselves\, connect with their environment\, and
  develop techniques and materials to decorate cave walls in Europe. Guided
  by Marlena Billings\, a PhD student in the Department of Anthropology\, t
 eens will explore examples of cave art and learn how archaeologists use ex
 perimental archaeology and microscopes to study how people manufactured ar
 t. Through hands-on activities\, participants will experiment with differe
 nt tools\, surfaces\, and light to see how ancient artists brought animals
  and scenes to life in dark cave spaces. Teen Saturdays Workshops are offe
 red bilingually in Spanish and English. They are designed to build communi
 ty and improve the museum experience for multicultural teens. Snacks provi
 ded! $10 fee includes free admission to all HMSC museums immediately follo
 wing the workshop. Teens will receive a free admission pass (worth $15) fo
 r a return visit if they attend one of the three sessions. October 17: Kna
 pping the First Tools: Teen Saturdays Workshop November 14: Making Paleoli
 thic Cave Art December 12: Animal Stories from the Past Presented by the P
 eabody Museum of Archaeology & Ethnology and the Harvard Museums of Scienc
 e & Culture. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: htt
 ps://www.meetboston.com/event/making-paleolithic-cave-art%3a-teen-saturday
 s-workshop/94147/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 
 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource pag
 e: https://www.meetboston.com/event/making-paleolithic-cave-art%3a-teen-sa
 turdays-workshop/94147/
LOCATION:Peabody Museum of Archaeology & Ethnology\, Harvard University\, 
 11 Divinity Ave\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/making-paleolithic-cave-art%3a-teen-s
 aturdays-workshop/94147/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:November Reception: Small Works 2026 and Drinks on Me
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261114T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T191221Z
UID:ad8639b06882a60ab10ab98b44b842@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our November Reception\, celebrating two new exhib
 itions at ArtsWorcester: The annual favorite Small Works\, and Amanda (And
 i) Pickler's solo exhibition Drinks on Me. Saturday\, November 14\, 2 - 5 
 PM ArtsWorcester\, 44 Portland St\, Worcester MA // Small Works 2026: A Me
 mbers' Exhibition This showcase of miniature works from ArtsWorcester arti
 st members\, ranging in theme and medium. All works are 10"x10" or under. 
 Do your holiday shopping (small works make unique\, wonderful gifts!) or c
 ome simply to explore these small treasures. // Amanda (Andi) Pickler: Dri
 nks on Me In Drinks on Me\, interdisciplinary artist Amanda (Andi) Pickler
  explores the spectrum of intimacy that exists within the domesticity of i
 nterpersonal relationships\, and the public and private spaces of queer ni
 ghtlife. Pickler's saturated\, jewel-toned paintings and detailed prints i
 nclude scenes from her trips to lesbian and queer bars around the country.
  These images and the spaces they depict offer connection\, joy\, and resp
 ite to a community experiencing significant challenges and threats. This e
 vent is free and open to all. Following the reception and beginning at 5:0
 0 PM\, an afterparty will be held at Femme Bar Worcester. Connect with the
  artist of Drinks on Me and see the Worcester bar that inspired some of An
 di's artworks. Small Works 2026 and Drinks on Me will be on view at ArtsWo
 rcester through December 13 during gallery hours: Wednesdays through Sunda
 ys\, each day from 12 PM to 5 PM (always free and open to all). On Decembe
 r 10\, ArtsWorcester will be open until 7PM for late night hours. Concurre
 ntly on view through the duration of the exhibition run will be the Assets
  for Artists 2026 Showcase\, on view in the third floor Davis Art Gallery.
  Parking is available at the Worcester Public Library (McGrath) Lot\, Fede
 ral Plaza Garage\, Worcester Common Garage\, and Pearl-Elm Garage. Metered
  street parking is also available. On weekends\, and on weekdays after 5:0
 0 PM\, visitors may park in the Printers Building parking lot free of char
 ge. Please do not park in the lot across the street from the Printers Buil
 ding\; you will be immediately towed. // Photos: Andi Pickler\, They Don't
  Get To Tell Us Whether Or Not This Is Real\, oil on canvas\, 48" x 26"\, 
 2026 Andi Pickler\, Our Hands At Ginger's\, oil on panel\, 14" x 18"\, 202
 5 Sarah Beard\, It Started to Clear Part Way Up\, 9" x 9"\, acrylic and co
 llage\, 2025 Marjorie Hart\, Hand woven purse with chain handle\, bamboo a
 nd cotton\, 8" x 8" x 0.5"\, 2024 Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts 
 Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/november-reception%3a-
 small-works-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31070/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mile
 s of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts
 -events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/november
 -reception%3a-small-works-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31070/
LOCATION:ArtsWorcester\, 44 Portland St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/november-reception%3a-small-wo
 rks-2026-and-drinks-on-me/31070/
END:VEVENT
