BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dust Bowls and Jewish Souls
DTSTART:20261116T000000
DTEND:20261116T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T191221Z
UID:f7146a69c249d04641a1647d826b12@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Doors open at 6:00pm Admission: $10 Documentary | USA 2026 | D
 irector: Steven Pressman | 89 min The name Woody Guthrie conjures images o
 f Dust Bowl families from the 1930s fleeing their soil-ravaged farms\, alo
 ng with those famous lyrical phrases\, “This land is your land\, this la
 nd is my land. From California to the New York Island.” However\, Woody'
 s horizons extended far beyond the dusty Oklahoma hills of his youth. Once
  his wanderings and ramblings brought him to New York City in the 1940s\, 
 he was introduced – both personally and professionally – into a vibran
 t Jewish culture that he wholeheartedly embraced and ultimately had a deep
  influence on his life and his music. Dust Bowls and Jewish Souls also wea
 ves in the story of Aliza Greenblatt\, an immigrant from Ukraine who later
  became a prominent Yiddish poet and songwriter -- and who also happened t
 o be Woody's mother-in-law. From the dust storms of Oklahoma to the lox an
 d bagels of Coney Island\, discover a whole new side of Woody Guthrie that
  will forever change your view of one of America’s most celebrated songw
 riters and cultural icons. Plan to stay for the conversation following the
  film. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.dis
 covercentralma.org/event/dust-bowls-and-jewish-souls/31309/\n\nEvents Near
  Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback
  from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma
 .org/event/dust-bowls-and-jewish-souls/31309/
LOCATION:Worcester JCC\, Worcester JCC 633 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA
 \, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/dust-bowls-and-jewish-souls/31
 309/
END:VEVENT
